 is a uniform deterministic algorithm\nthat constructs a feasible schedule of minimum makespan.\nGiven also an integer deadline \\(1\\le T\\le n\\), it decides feasibility\nexactly and returns a schedule whenever the answer is affirmative.\nBoth tasks can be performed in\n\\(O((L+2)^{150020})\\) steps on a deterministic multitape Turing machine,\nwhere \\(L\\) is the total binary input length."},{"appendix":false,"contribution_target":{"fingerprint":"sha256:1cc69a29a75e3e847ff9a0c51fa0733451f1cf5bbb7920fce1145102770a4b8c","grain":"paper-statement","id":"A-polynomial-time-algorithm-for-three-machine-unit-job-scheduling-September-24-2026#prop:algorithm","title":"prop:algorithm"},"credit":{"kind":"producer-declared","license":null,"license_status":"consult-source-notice","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","repository":"https://github.com/openai/math","source":"lean/formalization.yaml","source_registry":"index.json#/sources"},"detail":{"path":"../rows/1fd56b6e71a11d37b5b046c9.json","pointer":"/row"},"display":"Proposition","id":"r:A-polynomial-time-algorithm-for-three-machine-unit-job-scheduling-September-24-2026:prop:algorithm","manuscript_id":"p:A-polynomial-time-algorithm-for-three-machine-unit-job-scheduling-September-24-2026","name":"prop:algorithm","printed_number":"3.1","printed_number_provenance":{"atlas_pin":"598384f431d532144d03cbabd1c5b384e1610218","binding":{"file":"build/paper.tex","label":"prop:algorithm","line":374,"manuscript":"A-polynomial-time-algorithm-for-three-machine-unit-job-scheduling-September-24-2026","statement_sha256":"39eb4a0ca8424e93396fe3564556fd1d19d8b8563fab5e4169d578fc94c0c943"},"blob_sha256":"sha256:253ae0683558fd095a71d6f47ab0694d8d98b846c1a65d2bbf9b145d484af567","kind":"reading-page-computed","pdf_verified":false,"pin":"598384f431d532144d03cbabd1c5b384e1610218","renderer":"scripts/build_papers.py","source":"data/statement_numbers.json","upstream_pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb"},"printed_number_status":"r